# interplay_dag_program_order_same_task: Same-FIFO program order orders GPU work when the execs share a task, with no barrier between them. Child 1 carries opcode 99 (it faults), then exec A, which runs inc_k 800 times on a counter in one compute pass, then exec B, which copies the counter out, both on task 1 (B as opcode 55): they run behind the faulted head, one command buffer after the other on the task's queue (in-process the device's exec queue; in the service the task's), and Metal orders them on the counter buffer they share. The guest waits for B's copy to read 800 (guest memory: the stamps are held behind the fault, so no stamp can say B finished, and none is published alone, so the interrupt count is fixed). 0x1028 = 1 then publishes all three stamps in one interrupt. The same pair on two tasks is not ordered (the module's docstring), and is not locked.
